      "text": "To find the largest $t$ value at which the temperature was exactly 77 degrees, we set the given temperature equation equal to 77 and solve for $t$:\n\\begin{align*}\n-t^2 + 12t + 50 &= 77 \\\\\nt^2 - 12t + 27 &= 0\n\\end{align*}\nWe can factor this quadratic equation as:\n\\begin{align*}\n(t-3)(t-9) &= 0\n\\end{align*}\nSetting each factor equal to zero gives us two possible solutions for $t$:\n\\begin{align*}\nt - 3 &= 0 \\Rightarrow t = 3 \\\\\nt - 9 &= 0 \\Rightarrow t = 9\n\\end{align*}\nTherefore, the largest $t$ value at which the temperature was exactly 77 degrees is $\\boxed{9}$.The answer is: 9",
